WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:06.510
<i>In order to save Shingetsu, we entered Barian on board the Different Dimension Airship.</i>

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.770
<i>But the location we arrived at is Sargasso.</i>

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.780
<i>And what we saw there was Shingetsu's beaten body!</i>

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.240
<i>Shaking with anger, Yuma, along with Shark and Kaito,</i>

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.720
<i>started their Duels with Vector and his team!</i>

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.660
<i>But what was waiting for us was...!</i>

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.610
Yuma!

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.050
Ryouga! What in the world just happened?

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.010
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.330
What was...?

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.400
A Field Magic, huh?

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.770
That's right! This place is a Field Magic!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:51.230
The effect of Ancient Battlefield of the Different Dimension - Sargasso has been active since the beginning!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:53.190
What did you say?!

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.030
Right indeed, as planned, you went and Xyz Summoned without having the <i>slightest clue</i>!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.990
So it really was a trap!

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.000
According to Sargasso's effect, when an Xyz Monster is Special Summoned,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.710
you take 500 points of damage!

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.660
One more thing. A player who has an Xyz Monster out on the field

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.420
will also take 500 points of damage at the end of their turn!

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.340
Then after this, the three of them will...

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.560
...be certain to receive 500 points of damage, or not!

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.390
To summarize, during this turn alone,
 they'll take 1000 points of damage!

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:31.400
I see. So it's a Duel with the risk of continuously being damaged.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.360
Sounds like fun!

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.820
Did my little <i>present</i> for you make you <i>happy</i>?!

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.490
But the conditions are the same for them. Just what are they...?

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.890
Screw you!

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.730
No matter what traps are waiting for us, I'll definitely kick your ass!

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.270
You did that to Shingetsu... Shingetsu...

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.500
You won't get away with it!

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.590
<i>That</i> I'm looking <i>forward</i> to...

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.050
Right?

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.010
<i>He's</i> cheering you as well!

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.010
Stop it!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.570
Yuma! Calm down!

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.440
If you give in to your anger, you're doing just what he wants you to!

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.650
Shit! I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.610
I set one card and end my turn!

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.630
They ended their turns, so Sargasso's effect will...!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.750
Ahh! Foolma and the inferior shark were...!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.630
I activate Emperor Galaxion's effect!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.080
By detaching two Overlay Units,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:43.470
I can Special Summon Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon from my deck!

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.810
Darkness shining through the galaxy!

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.370
Become the Embodiment of Light and obey me as my servant!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.780
Come to me, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.490
I set one card and end my turn.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.530
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:10.660
Kaito too...!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.630
Good friends taking the same damage!

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.080
My turn! Draw!

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.370
I Summon Umbral Ghoul!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.990
And then I activate Umbral Ghoul's effect!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.030
By making this card's Attack Power zero,

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.440
I can Special Summon an Umbral Monster with zero Attack Power from my hand!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.150
Come! Two Umbral Will-o'-the-Wisps!

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.710
And then I activate Umbral Will-o'-the-Wisp's effect!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.910
When this card is Special Summoned,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.970
I can change one Monster's level to the same level as it!

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.420
So they become Level Fours!

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.450
Three Level Four Monsters...!

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:57.130
It's coming!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:04.590
I Overlay the Level Four Umbral Ghoul
 and the two Will-o'-the-Wisps!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.590
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.270
Xyz Summon!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.530
Come on out! Number 104!

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.350
Within this glaring holy light,

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.590
bring these foolish insects to their knees as they bow!

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.240
Masquerade Magician - Shining!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.480
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:39.450
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.160
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.510
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:57.590
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.100
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.470
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.690
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:12.230
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.360
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.070
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.530
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.580
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.040
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:31.080
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.840
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.300
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:40.010
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:49.060
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.710
So you finally played your Over-Hundred Number!

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:08.380
But now he'll take 500 damage from Sargasso's effect!

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:08.380
"Vector's Madness: 
The Battle Aboard the Ominous Sargasso!"

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.970
I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Sargasso's Lighthouse!

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.810
When I take damage from Sargasso's effect,

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:21.230
by sending this card to the Graveyard, that damage is negated,

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.150
Then, as long as this card remains in the Graveyard,

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.940
I won't receive Sargasso's effect!

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:28.700
N-No way...!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.910
So he took measures with a defense plan...

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.920
So that means Yuma and the others are the only ones who will take damage at the end of their turns?!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.630
That's not fair!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.340
Squirm within this Sargasso! <i>Suffer</i>!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.760
Go, Shining! Attack Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.640
I won't let that happen!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.890
I activate Hope's effect! Moon Barrier!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.020
You <i>fool</i>!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:00.350
What?!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.690
Shining's effect activates!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.110
By detaching an Overlay Unit,

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.650
it can negate the opponent's Monster's 
effects activated during battle!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.450
And <i>then</i>, as a <i>special favor</i>...

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.370
...the opposing player will take 800 damage!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:18.910
Yuma!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.630
Ain't done yet! Hope's effect was negated!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.590
Shining's attack will continue!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.880
Trap, activate! Half Unbreak!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:34.510
This card prevents a Monster from being destroyed through battle,

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.390
and halves the damage the player receives!

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.150
Whoa, whoa! You sure are <i>tough</i>!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.110
<i>If I at least have Hope left, then Hope Ray V can...!</i>

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.070
Well, if it's still here, the enjoyment will only <i>increase</i>!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.080
I set one card face-down! Turn end!

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:03.710
Just you watch! I swear I'm gonna beat you to a pulp just like you did him!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:04.210
Yuma!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.380
I'm gonna win this and get revenge for Shingetsu!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.170
Just calm down, Yuma!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.630
Shut up! You don't understand how I feel!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.590
Because of me, Shingetsu was...

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.760
Shingetsu!

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.730
My turn! Draw!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.940
I Summon Holy Lightning - Wings!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.950
And I activate Wings' effect!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.950
When this card is Summoned successfully,

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.950
I can Special Summon one Holy Lightning Monster from my hand!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.790
Come out, Holy Lightning - Books!

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.790
That makes two.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.760
I then activate Books' effect!

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:55.720
Once per turn, by sending 
a Magic Card from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.220
I can Special Summon one Holy Lightning Monster from my hand!

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.270
The card I send to the Graveyard is Sargasso's Lighthouse!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.150
And I Special Summon Holy Lightning - Sword from my hand!

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.240
He's got that card that negates Sargasso's effect!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.740
That's really cheap!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:23.330
Call it however you like. I must save the Barian World at any cost!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.080
Save?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.710
Those excuses aside,

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.250
I think you've given Ryouga a decent handicap here.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.000
Wouldn't you agree?

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.760
Yeah, that's right!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.590
Then, Ryouga, I'll come at you without holding back!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:42.720
I Overlay the Level Four Holy Lightning - Wings, Book, and Sword!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.520
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.310
Xyz Summon!

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.030
Show yourself, Number 102!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.450
Holy Lightning - Glorious Halo!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:05.700
That's...!

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.420
Hmph, so you finally came.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.750
My turn! Draw!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.970
When my opponent has a Monster on the field with more than 2000 Attack Points,

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.760
I can Special Summon this Monster!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:24.270
Show yourself, Schwarzschild, the Limit Dragon!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.480
<i>Level Eight...</i>

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.360
Then, when I have a Level Eight Monster on my field,

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.240
I can Summon Parsec, the Interstellar Dragon without release!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:44.830
I Overlay the Level Eight Schwarzschild, the Limit Dragon and Parsec, the Interstellar Dragon!

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.210
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.290
Xyz Summon!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.710
Manifest before us, Number 107!

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.180
Galaxy-Eyes Tachyon Dragon!

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:15.190
You don't have a card that negates the damage?

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.650
No, of course I have it.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.570
But that's a card for <i>cowards</i> to use!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.780
There's no meaning to this
 if I'm not in the same position as you!

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.460
This will determine which of us is the true Galaxy-Eyes user,

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.920
in a battle between two animals for their very existence!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.380
Very well.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.880
Shingetsu...

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.640
My turn! Draw!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.720
I use the Rank-Up Magic, Limited Barian's Force!

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.180
Wait, Yuma!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.680
Wh-Why are you stopping me?!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:54.900
If you Chaos Xyz Summon, we'll lose more Life Points because of Sargasso's effect!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.400
Even so, if this keeps up...

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.990
we'll lose 500 points at the end of our turn!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.160
We'll use Hope Ray V to settle this in one hit!

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.620
But Yuma, there's something strange about this Duel...

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:07.910
Strange?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:08.740
Yeah.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.330
It feels as though he's luring us...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.790
It's much different from the last time we fought Vector.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.960
Astral, if I get scared here, I can't honor Shingetsu!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.050
Stay calm, Yuma!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.840
Shut up!

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.890
They're fighting, or not?!

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.350
It's almost like the two of them aren't breathing at all!

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:33.850
I activate the Rank-Up Magic, Limited Barian's Force!

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.020
Yuma!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:39.400
This card evolves my Xyz Monster into a Chaos Xyz Monster!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.740
I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope to rebuild the Overlay Network!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.580
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:54.420
It's time to show yourself, Chaos Number 39!

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.880
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray V!

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.010
Hope Ray V!

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.140
It's here!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.140
So you made it, Hope Ray V.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.850
<i>But</i> you take 500 points of damage for doing that!

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:19.320
Yuma!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:25.030
I-I activate Hope Ray V's effect!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.330
Once per turn, by releasing one Overlay Unit,

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.830
I can destroy one Monster on the field,

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:36.330
and deal that Monster's total Attack Power as damage to my opponent!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.080
Shingetsu...

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.130
I swear to get revenge for you!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.720
Go, Hope Ray V!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.300
Shining Strike Slice!

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.020
Hope Sword V Blade Shoot!

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.350
Shining can only negate the effects of the opponent's Monsters during battle!

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.650
He did it!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.990
All he needs to do is direct attack the opponent and Yuma wins, or not!

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:11.580
Wait a minute.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.160
Just what's going on here?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.120
He... Vector is...

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.920
Vector just disappeared!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:28.590
Could that attack just now
 have sent him flying into another dimension?

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.640
No way... Then... I won?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.260
Shingetsu...

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:36.730
But Shingetsu is...

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.810
Shingetsu's already...

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.110
He won't come back!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:50.700
Thank you...

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.240
Yuma-<i>kun</i>...

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:55.660
Could it be...?!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:01.960
Shingetsu? You... You...!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.000
You're still alive?!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.210
Shingetsu!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.680
You're still alive, Shingetsu!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.940
Just <i>kidding</i>!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.280
S-Shingetsu?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.160
It's so funny my <i>stomach hurts</i>!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.200
What are you saying?!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.160
You sure are an interesting fellow.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.450
You really cared for me...!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.500
Then shall I <i>show you</i>?!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.090
Something <i>far more interesting</i>!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.090
Barial Force!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.090
What?!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.940
YUMA!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:18.660
You're...?!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.250
Vector?!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.790
Are you trying to impersonate Shingetsu?!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.300
In that case, then, where's the <i>real </i>Shingetsu?!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.880
"Real"? Who might <i>that</i> be?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.510
I'm <i>Vector</i>.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.260
You're so slow! <i>I'm Shingetsu</i>!

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.140
That can't be!

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.100
I mean, just a second ago Vector was Dueling me!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:46.860
And just the other day,
 Vector was Dueling me while Shingetsu was...

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.820
You <i>still</i> don't get it?!

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:54.530
The one Dueling the other day...
 The one Dueling just a moment ago...

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.990
It was a mere <i>clone</i> I created!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:03.460
The <i>real me</i> took the form of Rei Shingetsu, your close friend!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.920
Tada-da-da!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.000
Time to reveal the <i>shocking truth</i>!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.670
Man, that sure was some <i>trouble</i>!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.800
Having to play along with you as some <i>dense transfer student</i>!

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.300
N-No way...

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.600
Shingetsu's a Barian?!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.310
What a makeshift method.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.440
But <i>god</i> are you simple-minded!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:31.570
I spouted nothing but <i>nonsense</i> from my mouth, but you believed <i>every single word</i>!

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.820
"I'll protect Astral"?!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.070
"Barian <i>Police</i>"?!

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:44.960
<i>God</i> was it <i>fun</i>, <i>playing friends</i> with you!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.500
"Good work saving me back there."

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.670
"Officer Yuma"!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.670
Stop joking...

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.130
You can't be Shingetsu!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:59.090
He's... He's not the kind of guy who would trick people!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.180
Then I'll tell you!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:08.060
You've got five cards in your deck that represents the <i>proof of our friendship</i>, right?!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.980
<i>I'm lending you these cards.</i>

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.650
What did you say?!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.280
Don't tell me...! Yuma, did you know this?!

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.160
That Shingetsu was a Barian?!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:23.990
Yuma!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.790
Astral, that's...

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:33.550
Didn't tell him, did ya?
 Because they're tied together by your <i>solid friendship</i>...

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.300
...from your <i>dear friend, Shingetsu</i>!

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.050
Yuma!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.930
Yuma... Astral...

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:53.150
Thank you for protecting our friendship
 and <i>not telling the others</i>!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.030
Damn you!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.740
I Direct Attack with Hope Ray V!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.030
GO!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:10.460
Then I activate the Continuous Trap Card, Vain - Sneer of Betrayal!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.130
When a Monster with V in its name attacks,

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.420
that attack is <i>negated</i>!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:21.800
All the V cards in the opponent's deck are sent to the Graveyard!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:31.520
And for every V Monster sent to the Graveyard from the opponent's hand or deck,

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:36.440
I recover my Life by 500 for each V card sent!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.030
I just sent five cards to the Graveyard!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.700
Thus, I regain 2500 Life Points!

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.120
So he can actually regain his own Life by the amount of damage we take...

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.170
I'm not done! And <i>then</i>...

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.960
for each V card sent to the Graveyard,

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.170
my opponent must send five cards to the Graveyard!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:01.880
Five cards per each?!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:02.840
Then that means...!

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:06.390
Yuma!

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.100
Yuma has to send 25 cards to the Graveyard!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:18.360
No, not just 25! In total, you've sent 30 cards to the Graveyard!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.530
Deck Destruction, huh?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.490
Deck Destruction...

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:25.660
You've only got three cards left...!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.370
Being unable to draw a card
 means the same thing as losing the Duel!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.000
Human emotions are despicable.
 I'll dry them up bit-by-bit!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.130
Damn you!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:42.170
So having your clone Duel against Yuma

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.090
was your aim from the very start?!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.300
That's right!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.640
We're talking about Yuma here!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.770
I gave him those cards as proof of our friendship,

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.270
so he'd be sure to have them in his deck.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:59.270
<i>And</i> if I had him think I'd killed off Shingetsu, he'd lose his cool!

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:03.070
And I thought he'd be sure to attack with Hope Ray V!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.990
And what a guy you are! It <i>feels great</i> when someone <i>moves to your every whim</i>!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.460
It's the <i>best</i>! The <i>greatest</i>!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.290
Yuma...

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.510
<i>Now</i> then...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:28.470
Yuma, what're ya gonna <i>do</i> with <i>only three cards left to play</i>?!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.220
Why not show me the <i>best you can do</i>?!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:35.350
None of you will be crossing this path <i>alive anyway</i>!

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:40.650
And everything, Yuma, is because I <i>lured you here</i>!

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:44.110
You went and involved people who have nothing to do with this!

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:47.200
Me? I involved everyone...?

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:53.330
You were probably thinking it was... <i>intended for the best</i>!

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:01.750
Yuma...

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:24.570
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:32.240
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:39.830
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:47.170
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:47.720 --> 00:23:04.110
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:08.900
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:19.250
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:27.800
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:32.590
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:38.890
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:43.770
We've been cornered by Vector's lowly trap!

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:45.730
And we only have three cards left!

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:46.900
If this keeps up...!

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.040
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:05.790
"Countdown to Defeat!
 The Terror of Deck Destruction"

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:08.130
Astral... Just what are you...?!
